rly impossible to show in writing the longing which Christ our Lord unworthily communicates to me — which might be to me a pain and a torment, seeming on the one hand not to satisfy the vocation fully on my part, though on the other hand it consoles me to have communicated it to Your Paternity, whose care I experience every day, how great it is toward me, most unworthy son — that care which seeks every means for my salvation. Into the hands of Your Paternity, therefore, I commit myself wholly, and at every nod of yours I am ready to obey; and if you wished to try this with mortification and with public and outward penances, I am ready to receive them."
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
